          "text": "On admission he was febrile (38.6), tachypnoeic (RR 26), and hypoxic (sats 89% on room air) with coarse crackles at the right base. Chest X-ray confirmed right lower lobe consolidation; CRP was 180 and WCC 16. He was treated with IV co-amoxiclav and IV clarithromycin, controlled oxygen therapy, and IV fluids. An ITU review was undertaken on day 2, at which point a ceiling of care was agreed as ward-based in view of his COPD severity and frailty; a family meeting was also held on day 2. Antibiotics were stepped down to oral on day 3. By day 5, sats had improved to 93% on room air.",
